language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Graceful labelling of a graph with n nodes and m edges: the nodes get distinct labels from 0 to m, and the edge labels |f(x) - f(y)| are all different. Print the node labels and the edge labels.
given n : int(1..)
given m : int(1..)
given graph : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..2)] of int(0..n-1)
find nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..m)
find edges : matrix indexed by [int(1..m)] of int(1..m)

branching on [nodes]

such that
$ each node gets its own label from 0 to m
allDiff(nodes),
$ each edge is labelled with the absolute difference of the labels of its two end nodes (graph gives 0-based node numbers)
forAll e : int(1..m) . (edges[e] = |nodes[graph[e,1] + 1] - nodes[graph[e,2] + 1]|),
$ the edge labels are all different
allDiff(edges)
